  ;; jolt-2j3 — the protocol-map keys jolt deliberately does NOT carry. These are
  ;; jolt-side rows, not corpus rows: the reference DOES set every one of them, so
  ;; a corpus row here would only be a certified divergence. What they pin is that
  ;; the omission stays deliberate and stays complete.
  ;;
  ;; :on / :on-interface / :method-builders describe the interface the reference's
  ;; defprotocol generates (my.ns/P yields the interface my.ns.P). jolt generates
  ;; none — dispatch is by the receiver's type tag (protocols.ss protocol-resolve)
  ;; — so there is no name to report and no Class to hand back.
  {:suite "defprotocol-value" :expr "(do (defprotocol Pu1 \"d\" (mu1 [this])) (sort (keys Pu1)))" :expected "(:doc :method-map :methods :name :sigs :var :jolt/type)"}
